              <div class="stat"><div class="n">152</div><div class="l">passing tests (Warvis)</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">0.84&rarr;0.99</div><div class="l">Kiln eval score</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/ashmitbohora" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="GitHub profile: Warvis and Kiln">GitHub profile →</a></div>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="4" id="shipped">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#B93018"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 05</b> · Special sauce · Shipped</span></span>
            <h2>Shipped Production Apps</h2>
            <p class="lead">Guruji and BohoQuest: <span>real users, real database, real tests.</span></p>
            <p class="body">Guruji (getguruji.com): a gamified learning PWA (React, TypeScript, Supabase) with RLS-scoped auth and a self-run security audit against the live database, zero exploitable vulnerabilities. BohoQuest (app.bohoquest.app): a gamified check-in app (Expo/React Native) with server-side anti-cheat, Apple Sign-In, and a 121-test suite, live in TestFlight.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">exploitable vulns found</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">121</div><div class="l">BohoQuest test suite</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">TestFlight</div><div class="l">live status</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="links">
              <a href="https://getguruji.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">getguruji.com →</a>
              <a href="https://app.bohoquest.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">app.bohoquest.app →</a>
            </div>
